  "notes": [
    "P3.3 quoted sha256 679fe331... as the pin for artifacts/candidates.jsonl. That pin in release/MANIFEST.jsonl is STALE and was stale before this branch: the artifact moved 679fe331 -> b74576fa (3de10b7) -> 5113ad32 (c6a5b82), and c6a5b82 is an ancestor of this run's base. The condition read literally was unsatisfiable when written; it was scored on intent (E15 must not move the hash) and passes -- 5113ad32 stable across four regenerations. The stale pin is a live manifest-stale break for the release track and was reported, not touched.",
    "M30 survivor was acted on: the success/status disagreement guard was one-directional. status==0 with success false fell through to result.x and minted a Certificate from a failed solve, which check_exactly would then report as a CertificateError -- i.e. as weights that failed re-checking rather than as a solve that never succeeded. Guard made symmetric; the refusal now carries a rebuilt undecided outcome so a caller cannot read decided=True off a refusal.",
    "A mutation battery running in this shared worktree left live mutants in tracked source during the run. Two subagents reported phantom suite failures (13 and 2) caused by them. All numbers here were taken on a tree verified clean by git diff immediately before and after.",
    "The three *.stdout.txt captures were normalised to LF before hashing: .gitattributes pins LF, so hashing the working-tree CRLF bytes would have recorded sha256s that no committed blob has -- the same defect as the stale release pin reported above, and it would have been self-inflicted."
  ],
